---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const description = 'Fasolati connects oral health, gut context, and host response through an evidence-led research program. Explore the Life Board concept and OMV science spine.';
---
<Base title="Fasolati | Oral health, in the whole picture" description={description} path="/" interior={false}>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="h-label mo">Oral · Gut · Systemic</p>
    <h1 class="h1 mo mo-d1">Fasolati<sup>™</sup></h1>
    <p class="h-tag mo mo-d2">“Oral health is the last unlit corner of systemic health.”</p>
    <p class="h-sub mo mo-d3">We’re building a clearer picture of how oral health fits into the health of the whole person. Simple enough to use. Deep enough to question.</p>
    <p class="h-mic mo mo-d4">An evidence-led platform in development</p>
    <div class="h-btns mo mo-d4">
      <a class="btn bp" href="/science/">Explore the science spine</a>
      <a class="btn bs" href="#s4">Meet the Life Board</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section" id="s1">
    <div class="section-kicker">The proposition</div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <h2>The mouth belongs<br />in the picture.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Periodontal treatment can improve some systemic markers in defined patient groups. A Cochrane review found improved blood-glucose control in people with both diabetes and periodontitis. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35420698/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the clinical review</a>.</p>
        <p>That is a reason to investigate the connection, not permission to attribute every inflammatory signal to the mouth. Fasolati’s question is more specific: can we measure something about oral bacterial activity that adds useful information beyond a periodontal exam and bacterial count?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section" id="framework">
    <div class="section-kicker">The science spine</div>
    <h2>Four questions.<br />No invisible leaps.</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">A research map, not a proven chain in an individual. Each step needs its own measurement and evidence.</p>
    <div class="question-map">
      <a href="/science/#measurement"><span class="map-index">01 / Source ecology</span><h3>What is there?</h3><p>Organisms, bacterial burden, and the local oral environment.</p><span class="map-link">Define the source ↗</span></a>
      <a href="/science/#mapping"><span class="map-index">02 / Effector activity</span><h3>What does it release?</h3><p>Vesicles, associated cargo, and other biologically active material.</p><span class="map-link">Explore the mechanisms ↗</span></a>
      <a href="/science/#human-evidence"><span class="map-index">03 / Delivered exposure</span><h3>What gets through?</h3><p>Material that reaches another compartment, with its source established.</p><span class="map-link">Examine the human bridge ↗</span></a>
      <a href="/science/#experiments"><span class="map-index">04 / Host response</span><h3>What changes?</h3><p>A separately measured response, and a test of whether the information helps.</p><span class="map-link">See the next experiments ↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <p class="boundary-note">An oral measurement is not a circulating concentration. A biological mechanism is not a personal disease-risk score.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section" id="s2">
    <div class="section-kicker">The oral research program</div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <h2>Beyond the<br />bacterial census.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Outer membrane vesicles, or OMVs, are one type of bacterial extracellular vesicle. Experimental studies show that periodontal-bacterial vesicles can carry active material and trigger different immune responses. <a href="https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0151967" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cecil et al., 2016</a>.</p>
        <p>Fasolati is interested in function as well as composition: not only which bacteria are present, but what their released material does. The first job is to establish exactly what an assay measures and whether vesicle-associated activity adds information.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/science/#mapping">Follow the OMV-to-effect map →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section" id="s3">
    <div class="section-kicker">The gut and systemic context</div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <h2>Connected does<br />not mean identical.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Human studies have characterized bacterial-vesicle-associated material in blood, including associations with intestinal-barrier dysfunction. They do not establish that a particular person’s circulating material came from the mouth. <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6943244/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tulkens et al.</a></p>
        <p>Our proposed architecture keeps oral observations, gut context, and host-response markers distinct. Agreement can suggest a question worth testing. Disagreement is information too, not something to hide inside a single score.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section life-board-section" id="s4">
    <div class="section-kicker">The Life Board / Product concept</div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <div><h2>Simple on the surface.<br />Inspectable underneath.</h2><p class="section-intro">The proposed Life Board is organized around three questions, not a mysterious health number. This is a design direction, not a live clinical dashboard.</p><a class="text-link" href="/engine/">Explore the Life Board concept →</a></div>
      <div class="board-concept">
        <div class="board-head"><span>Fasolati / Life Board</span><span>Concept</span></div>
        <div class="board-row"><span>01</span><div><h3>What changed?</h3><p>The actual measurement, its date, and a comparable prior result. Missing data stays missing.</p></div></div>
        <div class="board-row"><span>02</span><div><h3>How sure are we?</h3><p>Measurement quality and repeatability, kept separate from the strength of the underlying science.</p></div></div>
        <div class="board-row"><span>03</span><div><h3>What is the next justified step?</h3><p>A useful question, a repeat measurement when warranted, or a conversation with a clinician.</p></div></div>
        <a href="/science/#life-board" class="board-evidence">Open the evidence rules ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sp-section" id="s5">
    <div class="section-kicker">Build with us</div>
    <div class="editorial-split">
      <h2>Earn every<br />connection.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>We’re looking for collaborators who can help test the hard parts: assay identity, source attribution, functional activity, and clinical usefulness. A result that changes the hypothesis is progress.</p>
        <p>Our oral-care and broader platform programs belong alongside that research, not ahead of it. Product-specific benefit must be established for the finished intervention and the intended use.</p>
        <div class="inline-actions"><a class="btn bp" href="/partner/">Start a conversation</a><a class="text-link" href="/platform/">Explore the programs →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
